; Tutorial_3_Find_a_Station.inix -- a station that may carry the Seahawks game: searched, filtered, narrowed, ordered, played and marked.

[about]
Title=3 - Find a Station
Intro=RadioTrail searched for words, filtered to the stations that mention the Seattle Seahawks, narrowed to Washington, put in order, and one played; then stations marked to keep.
Setup=DbDo is open on RadioTrail.
Homework=Filter RadioTrail for your own team or a favorite genre, then play what is left.

[step]

Say=One want: a station that may be carrying the Seattle Seahawks game, ready to play.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus D, D for DbDo, opens it or brings it forward.
Key=Alt+Control+D
Hear=DbDo
Hear=DbDo ready

[step]

Say=Control plus K, K for Keywords, searches every column for words: names, genres, notes, all of them.
Key=Control+K
Hear=Keywords dialog
Hear=Keywords: edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type seahawks and press Enter. The cursor moves to the first station that mentions the team.
Key=Enter
Hear=99.3 KDRM, Row 3290 of 55280
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=F3 goes to the next match, Shift plus F3 to the one before. Keywords moves the cursor and hides nothing. To see only the matches, filter.
Key=F3
Hear=CISL Sportsnet 650 Richmond, BC
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A planned misstep: Control plus F is not Find here. In DbDo, F is for Filter. Control plus F shows only the records that match, beginning with a choice offered as buttons.
Key=Control+F
Hear=Filter Records dialog
Hear=Any Field button
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Any Field is the first button, so Enter presses it. It asks for the text to find, wherever it is.
Key=Enter
Hear=Any Field Contains dialog
Hear=Text to find in any field: edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type seahawks and press Enter.
Key=Enter
Hear=7 records have seahawks.
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Seven: stations in Seattle and Tacoma, in British Columbia and in Idaho. Control plus F again; with a filter in force there are more buttons. N for Narrow keeps seahawks and adds a field.
Key=N
Hear=Filter Records dialog, name: edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I move to the state box, type Washington, and press Enter.
Key=Enter
Hear=Filter applied. 3 records match.
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Shift plus F, Say Filter, says both parts, in the words each was asked in.
Key=Shift+F
Hear=any field contains seahawks; and where: state = 'Washington'
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus O, O for Order, sorts by a column; I choose name, and Enter sorts.
Key=Alt+O
Hear=Order Records dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Down Arrow to the second.
Key=Down Arrow
Hear=KIRO 710 ESPN Seattle, Row 2 of 3
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The sports station. Alt plus Shift plus P plays it.
Key=Alt+Shift+P
Hear=Homer Player, KIRO 710 ESPN Seattle
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape. To keep stations, mark them. Control plus M, M for Mark, marks the station I am on, and Control plus Shift plus M unmarks: Shift reverses.
Key=Control+M
Hear=Marked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=For a run of records, F8 starts it where I am, and Shift plus F8 completes it where I stop. Control plus A marks every record in view.
Key=Control+A
Hear=Marked 3 records
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Now the payoff. With records marked, Alt plus Shift plus P plays all of them, one after another, as a playlist.
Key=Alt+Shift+P
Hear=Homer Player, 3 tracks, 99.3 KDRM
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape. Control plus Shift plus F clears the filter, and every station is back, the marks kept. Marks stay when DbDo closes, so a marked station is a favorite to come back to.
Key=Control+Shift+F
Hear=Filter cleared. 55280 records.
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I name the command; the reader gives the key.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Search every column.
Key=
Hear=Control plus K

[step]

Say=Show only the matches.
Key=
Hear=Control plus F

[step]

Say=Say the filter.
Key=
Hear=Shift plus F

[step]

Say=Order by a column.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus O

[step]

Say=Mark a record.
Key=
Hear=Control plus M

[step]

Say=Play the marked stations.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Shift plus P
